e real drift signal. A new release that moves nothing does not go red.\n- Not chosen: skipping the comparison when the release differs. That would turn the pin into a no-op on two of the three supported runtimes.\n- What remains: when CI's Node moves to a CLDR release that moves a first day, this pin goes red until the table or the ledger is updated. That is the drift the round asked to keep catching, and the failure message names both remedies.\n\n**Ablations on the new head**, each through `scripts/ablation-replace.mjs`, each with the mutation proven landed and the restore proven (`blob == HEAD`, `git diff HEAD` empty), and each run on all three runtimes:\n\n| Leg | Mutation | CLDR 46 | CLDR 47 | CLDR 48 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A4 | Iceland removed from the table (back to CLDR 47 content) | red: parity and ledger honesty | red: parity and ledger honesty | red: parity (CI's shape, `{ IS: 0 }` found) and ledger honesty |\n| A6 | the ledger's `47` row removed | green | red: `{ IS: 1 }` found, `{}` expected | green |\n| A3 | the CLDR table removed | 6 red | 6 red | 6 red |\n| A3b | the engine path skipped | 2 red | 2 red | 2 red |\n\n**Re-run at `a393686`** (after merging `main` at `da35453` in `98877dd`, a merge commit; no rebase, no force-push):\n- `pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 packages/i18n/ packages/plugin-calendar/ packages/plugin-timeline/` exited 0 on CLDR 47: 184 files, 2283 passed, 145 skipped. The same suites under Node 22.23.3 (CLDR 48, CI's release) exited 0 with the same counts.\n- `firstDayOfWeek-11675.test.ts` alone: 14 of 14 passed on CLDR 46, 47 and 48.\n- The zone driver `scripts/__tests__/date-only-zone-pins-10183.test.ts` exited 0, 27 passed.\n- `type-check` and `lint` for the three packages exited 0. The package warning totals are unchanged, and both edited files have 0 warnings.\n- `check:new-line-citations`, `check:control-bytes`, `check:changeset-claims`, `check:pending-changeset-literals`, `check-changeset-no-major`, `chec